## Final Judgement
## Summary of Key Findings

Multiple sources consistently confirm that Kamala Harris, who was indeed a U.S. Senator at the time of the claim (October 14, 2020), took the California bar exam in 1989 after graduating from UC Hastings College of the Law. Several sources—including Distractify, JD Advising, and a lawnews.tv op-ed by a classmate—explicitly state that she failed the bar exam on her first attempt and passed on her second try, being admitted to the California bar in June 1990. The evidence is clear, consistent across multiple sources, and directly addresses every component of the claim.

## Conclusion

The evidence from the fact-check directly and unambiguously supports the claim. Multiple independent sources confirm that Kamala Harris failed the California bar exam on her first attempt in 1989 before passing on her second attempt.

